{
  "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
  "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nDAVID WYCOFF, ESQ., Assistant Federal Defender, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nRONALD EISENBERG, ESQ., Deputy District Attorney, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Pace, at age 17, was sentenced to life without possibility of parole after being misled by his lawyer and the court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first petition raised only an ineffectiveness claim. The second petition raised a due process challenge to the colloquy, which was not exhausted in the first, raised new evidence to support the claim which Pennsylvania law allowed him to do, and raised a constitutional and State law challenge to the legality of his sentence. There were new claims in the second proceeding."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: I don't care what the Pennsylvania law is. I mean, it -- it seems to me if you have a statute that says it's untimely unless one of these three exceptions apply, and -- and you -- you simply file and you don't say -- and it's clearly out of time without one of the exceptions, and you simply file and don't say but this exception applies, it seems to me that's not properly filed, whatever the rule in -- in Pennsylvania was."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, Pennsylvania actually does that and certainly did it at the time Mr. Pace was litigating."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0000-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "AEDPA says we'll toll for properly filed applications. That -- AEDPA is keyed to how much process the State post-conviction courts will give you."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: I thought the whole purpose of AEDPA was -- was to prevent delay. I mean, that's -- that's what's -- it seems to me counter-intuitive about the position you're -- you're urging upon us."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the State's procedural filing requirements. This is a Federal statute and properly filed is given a Federal meaning, but you presumably look to the State filing requirements, as you did in Artuz, to determine what that means."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wycoff",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WYCOFF: The AEDPA prefiling requirement where you go to the court and you say, I'd like to file this petition, tell me if I can, and the court says, 30 days later, yes or no."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But if he had gone into the Federal court he went into, and he had not gone through this State procedure, he would have been turfed out."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You can't get equitable tolling, Your Honor, our position would be --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right. Let's suppose to get away from it -- can I go -- are you finished with equitable tolling because I want to go back to --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, the -- the Congress that passed this statute of limitations is the same Congress that made the decision about whether habeas petitioners would be appointed counsel or not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The incentive that they have to drag it on is that they may come up with a new legal theory that attracts a -- a court that they didn't present before, that new facts may come up, may arise that they try to argue."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I might lose those arguments, but I really thought I could win, and therefore you should give me equitable tolling while I pursue them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Pennsylvania",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In fact, Pennsylvania in the Lambert case, in their opposition to the certiorari petition in May of 1998, said that that's a correct statement of Pennsylvania law, that there are judicially created exceptions, including the miscarriage of justice exception which will probably apply to the time bar, just like they applied to the other statutory bars."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "State law was unclear."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9627",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "document_hash": "ccdd1549f07044d27a169b73d481a7b91931d7dc42373997615d0a2e816bc849",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ccdd1549f070-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Thank you, Mr. Wycoff. The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
